20:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"Freshness","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]," is a sealed interface with exactly five variants. There is no sixth fetching mode\nhiding elsewhere in the API."],"className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
21:["$","$L57",null,{"id":"cachedorfetch-the-default","children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"CachedOrFetch","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],": the default"]}]
22:["$","p",null,{"children":"Serve a locally available value immediately. Invalidated values and source-of-truth rows without\nfreshness metadata are served as stale while one background revalidation runs. Fetch when no\nlocal value exists. This is stale-while-revalidate, and it is the default shape of every read.\nMore on that below.","className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
23:["$","$L57",null,{"id":"maxagenotolderthan","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"MaxAge(notOlderThan)","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]}]
24:["$","p",null,{"children":["Serve a locally available value only when it has known freshness metadata, has not been\ninvalidated, and its age does not exceed ",["$","code",null,{"children":"notOlderThan","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],". Otherwise withhold it and fetch a fresh\nvalue."],"className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
25:["$","p",null,{"children":["One pitfall worth naming: a row hydrated by an external writer with no recorded freshness\nmetadata is ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"withheld"}]," under ",["$","code",null,{"children":"MaxAge","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],". The read fetches rather than serving it. If you want a\nmetadata-less row served while it refreshes, that is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"CachedOrFetch","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],"'s job."],"className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
26:["$","$L57",null,{"id":"mustbefresh","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"MustBeFresh","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]}]
27:["$","p",null,{"children":"Never serve a cached value. Block until a fresh fetch succeeds and fail when it does not. A\nsource-of-truth row without freshness metadata is also withheld.","className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
28:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"MustBeFresh","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]," is the one policy whose initial-cycle failure terminates a stream: an initial-cycle\nfetch or revalidation failure emits one error and completes the flow, where every other failure\nleaves the flow live. The full rules for which failures end a stream are on the\n",["$","a",null,{"href":"/docs/store6/concepts/read-contract","children":"read contract","className":"font-medium text-accent-strong underline decoration-separator decoration-1 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-accent-strong focus-visible:rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"}]," page."],"className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
29:["$","$L57",null,{"id":"staleiferror","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"StaleIfError","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]}]
2a:["$","p",null,{"children":"Prefer fresh data after invalidation or when a local value has no freshness metadata, but fall\nback to that stale value when the fetch fails. A local value with current known metadata is\nserved without fetching.","className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
2b:["$","p",null,{"children":["On ",["$","code",null,{"children":"get","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],", the difference from the default is blocking behavior: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"StaleIfError","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]," blocks after\ninvalidation and returns the resident value only when the refresh fails, whereas ",["$","code",null,{"children":"CachedOrFetch","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],"\nreturns the resident value immediately and refreshes it in the background."],"className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
2c:["$","$L57",null,{"id":"localonly","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"LocalOnly","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]}]
2d:["$","p",null,{"children":["Never invoke the fetcher. Serve only locally available data and report ",["$","code",null,{"children":"StoreError.Missing","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]," when\nnone exists. On a memory miss, the configured source of truth is probed once, so a pre-existing\npersisted row counts as locally available data. When nothing is resident anywhere, the read\nfails ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Missing","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]," without a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Loading","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]," frame and without calling the fetcher."],"className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
2e:["$","p",null,{"children":["Pitfall: the builder still requires a fetcher even if every read you ever issue is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"LocalOnly","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],".\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"store<K, V> { }","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}]," without one fails at build time with a message that says so. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"LocalOnly","className":"rounded-md bg-surface-secondary px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-foreground"}],"\nchanges what a read does, not what a store needs."],"className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
2f:["$","p",null,{"children":"The policy goes at the call site:","className":"my-4 leading-7 text-foreground"}]
5b:T749,<pre class="shiki store-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-keyword)">val</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)"> profile </span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-keyword)">=</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)"> users.</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-function)">get</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">(</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-function)">UserKey</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">(</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-string)">"1"</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">), Freshness.</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-function)">MaxAge</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">(5.minutes))</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">users.</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-function)">stream</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">(</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-function)">UserKey</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">(</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-string)">"1"</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">), Freshness.LocalOnly).</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-function)">collect</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)"> { result </span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-keyword)">-></span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-function)">  render</span><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">(result)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:var(--color-store-code-foreground)">}</span></span></code></pre>30:["$","$L58",null,{"className":"store-m-code store-m-code-slab","data-code-theme":"dark","children":[["$","$L59",null,{"className":"store-m-code-header","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-sm font-medium","children":"Per-call freshness"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-store-code-foreground/75 text-xs","children":"kotlin"}],["$","$L5a",null,{"code":"val profile = users.get(UserKey(\"1\"), Freshness.MaxAge(5.minutes))\n\nusers.stream(UserKey(\"1\"), Freshness.LocalOnly).collect { result ->\n  render(result)\n}"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"[&_.shiki]:m-0 [&_.shiki]:overflow-x-auto [&_.shiki]:bg-transparent [&_.shiki]:p-4 [&_.shiki]:font-mono [&_.shiki]:text-sm [&_.shiki]:leading-6","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$5b"}}]]}]
